| `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` | integer | `15000` | a whole number, 1 or more and at most `threading.TIMEOUT_MAX`, and at least `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds` plus twice `make_targets.gate_stop_grace_seconds` plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds` | `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`tool_limits`, `run_tool`) for `_run` in `agents/doc_reviewer`, `agents/index_enforcer`, `agents/practice_refactor` and `agents/wiki_navigator` `_brain.py`, and `_run_doer` in `mcp/action_server.py` | Sets how long one tool child an agent starts (a gate run, a corpus query, the gated apply), or the MCP action server's doer, may run before its whole session is sent SIGKILL and the call is refused as `ChildTimedOut` naming this key; `scripts/doc_review.py`, `scripts/refactor_practice.py` and `scripts/hooks/on_stop_doc_review.py` then exit 1, and the action server answers the tool call with an error. A value shorter than that is refused with exit 14 before the child starts, the line naming the least value accepted, because a timed-out gate run waits its grace once for make's session to end and once more for make's output, and because a tool child can be `scripts/run_make_target.py`, and a SIGKILL to it would cut make's SIGTERM grace short, lose the runner's structured result and leave an applied edit not rolled back. It is read from the tree the tool acts on, the one whose gate keys the gate runner reads: `--root` for `scripts/doc_review.py` and `scripts/refactor_practice.py` (this checkout when it is not given), and the served root for each MCP server. The MCP action and Q&A servers read it at start and refuse a bad value with exit 14 before they serve. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] agents.tool_timeout_seconds = 15000` to stderr. | a gate's own limit: `make_targets.gate_timeout_seconds`; a model call's: `models.timeout_seconds` | always |
